+2. CENTRAL VSS HYPOTHESIS
+
+The current defects may represent a broader class of problem:
+
+Marciale-OS often possesses the underlying state, intelligence, or capability but does not consistently expose, synchronize, verify or recover it across subsystem boundaries.
+
+Examples:
+
+State exists
+    ↓
+UI doesn't expose it
+Engine exists
+    ↓
+Engine lifecycle isn't normalized
+Audio works
+    ↓
+Audio lifecycle isn't coordinated
+Knowledge exists in TAMA
+    ↓
+Learning workflow doesn't fully exploit it
+Bridge exists
+    ↓
+Failure state isn't sufficiently observable
+Tests pass
+    ↓
+Commander-facing vertical slice still fails
+
+The audit must attempt to falsify this hypothesis.
+
+3. VSS-00 — SHARED RUNTIME / SYSTEM COHESION AUDIT
+
+This is the highest-level addition to the original audit.
+
+Before rebuilding individual subsystems, inspect the common infrastructure beneath them.
+
+3.1 HubFrame
+
+Audit:
+
+mount;
+unmount;
+reload;
+close;
+navigation;
+loading;
+error state;
+recovery;
+iframe lifecycle;
+postMessage behavior.
+
+TheHUB already treats HubFrame as a reusable abstraction for Companion and other embedded systems.
+
+A shared lifecycle bug could therefore produce apparently unrelated failures across IdleHero, ChessLab, RuView and future embedded systems.
+
+3.2 Bridge Contracts
+
+Audit all:
+
+postMessage events;
+acknowledgements;
+timeout behavior;
+stale receivers;
+destroyed frames;
+reconnections;
+duplicate messages;
+unknown messages;
+message ordering.
+
+The existing Companion architecture already distinguishes events such as:
+
+hub.activity
+hub.companion.snapshot
+hub.companion.event
+hub.companion.pause
+hub.companion.resume
+
+
+idlehero.ready
+idlehero.ack
+
+Therefore the next maturity step is formal lifecycle behavior when these contracts fail, not merely adding additional messages.
+
+3.3 Global Lifecycle
+
+Identify single owners for:
+
+audio;
+notifications;
+session state;
+iframe state;
+background activity;
+application visibility;
+AI context;
+cleanup.
+
+A page should request a capability.
+
+It should not independently govern the lifetime of a global service.
